WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.106
Trace the liquid from the vessel through
the outlet and transfer hose.

2
00:00:04.226 --> 00:00:09.005
Include impeller surfaces, seals, gaskets
and valve seats, not just

3
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:10.416
the vessel shell.

4
00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:13.565
The diagram marks these as one contact
path.

5
00:00:13.685 --> 00:00:17.679
A statement that the vessel is stainless
steel leaves elastomers and

6
00:00:17.799 --> 00:00:19.869
purchased components unresolved.

7
00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:24.895
Ask how each material is identified and
justified for the product, cleaning

8
00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:29.410
agents, temperature and contact time
relevant to the intended use.

9
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:34.830
A material certificate can support
identity, but identity alone does not

10
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.238
prove compatibility with a specific
formulation or cleaning regime.

11
00:00:39.358 --> 00:00:43.753
Similarly, a surface-finish number is
useful only with a justified

12
00:00:43.873 --> 00:00:46.902
requirement and a defined verification
method.

13
00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:51.438
This introductory module does not
prescribe a universal steel grade,

14
00:00:51.558 --> 00:00:53.606
roughness value or elastomer.

15
00:00:53.726 --> 00:00:58.227
In the fictional review, mark the gasket
compatibility statement missing and

16
00:00:58.347 --> 00:01:02.422
request product-specific evidence from the
responsible specialists.

17
00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:07.117
The design sketch contrasts a clear outlet
path with a pocket that

18
00:01:07.237 --> 00:01:08.666
may retain liquid.

19
00:01:08.786 --> 00:01:12.178
Review access, cleaning coverage,
disassembly needs,

20
00:01:12.298 --> 00:01:13.919
drainage and inspection.

21
00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:17.856
Consider whether maintenance can be
performed without creating an

22
00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:20.195
uncontrolled product-quality risk.

23
00:01:20.315 --> 00:01:25.157
A favourable drawing is only a design
argument: cleaning effectiveness still

24
00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:27.923
needs the applicable validation evidence.

25
00:01:28.043 --> 00:01:33.141
Do not copy a hygienic-design ratio from
another application and present it

26
00:01:33.261 --> 00:01:35.480
as a universal GMP rule.

27
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.729
Our worked finding is specific: the outlet
drawing shows a retained pocket

28
00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:42.513
with no cleaning rationale.

29
00:01:42.633 --> 00:01:47.711
Record the drawing revision and location,
request a revised arrangement or a

30
00:01:47.831 --> 00:01:51.009
justified control strategy, and assign an
owner.

31
00:01:51.129 --> 00:01:55.183
Link the response to installation
inspection and the cleaning study.

32
00:01:55.303 --> 00:01:58.631
Avoid a vague action such as improve
cleanability.

33
00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:03.679
A closed action needs reviewed evidence
that addresses the actual concern,

34
00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:06.188
not merely an email saying resolved.
